            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Simple and delicious! Just as the submitter states this is definitely a nice alternative to bottled italian dressings for a marinade. I used olive oil instead of vegetable oil and a mix of white wine vinegar and regular distilled white and cut back a bit on the water. I did add the poultry seasoning and marinated this overnight. I added a sprig of fresh rosemary to this while it was grilling. This chicken was exceptionally good and I will definitely make this again."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Penelope"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The whole family enjoyed. I used 1/4 c water,1/3 c vinegar, 1/3 olive oil, 1 1/ tsp thyme and rosemary, 1 tsp basil &amp; oregano, 1 tbsp jarred low sodium chicken bouillon instead of poultry seasoning,1 tsp low sodium salt , 1/2 tsp white pepper. Place in a blender for a seconds to mix well and marinaded chicken for 4 hours, then grilled. Nice alternative to bottled.",
            "datePublished": "2025-11-10T23:58:27.631Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "OddGum6569"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'm making this tomorrow! Going to use a white wine vinegar and avocado oil, reduce the amount of Italian seasoning, and replace the dried thyme and rosemary with fresh thyme, rosemary and sage. I may also add the smallest, tiniest pinch of chilli powder/cayenne pepper to elevate the flavors. Can't wait!",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-03T23:55:10.403Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "foodlvr"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I marinated vegetables (carrots, onions, zucchini, and yellow squash) in this marinade, and then grilled on indoor griddle pan and served over wild rice. My family loved it, and my husband asked for me to make it again! Quick, easy, low fat, and delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2009-12-28T16:13:19.440Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cbrown"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great marinade. So easy to make. I used white wine vinegar instead of the white vinegar and olive oil instead of vegetables oil.",
            "datePublished": "2021-07-19T15:36:50.877Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I subbed lemon juice for vinegar and apple juice for water (I was out of white wine vinegar and wanted to use up the apple juice). Used all the herbs and marinated cubed chicken for about 5 hrs, threaded them onto skewers alternating with big zucchini pieces and grilled for about 15 minutes brushing with the marinade. I actually got MMMMMs at the table! This is definitely going into the rotation. Thank you Denyse for a great recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-17T11:53:27.480Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "hungryhippo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "followed recipe as best as i could (didn't have rosemary or italian seasoning, but used oregano/basil/parsley/garlic). i swapped olive oil for veggie oil. marinaded 2 breast halves for 8 hours. cooked them at 350 for 40 mins on foil-covered metal pan til it reached 165 degrees. moist and delicious! tasted like italian dressing, but maybe healthier?",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-05T19:17:14.520Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dandylicious"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great marinade for chicken, I kept to the recipe except that I used white wine vinegar instead of regular vinegar...added a wonderful depth to the taste of the chicken. Used this marinade for a baked chicken recipe. Thanks for sharing.",
            "datePublished": "2014-11-01T10:08:51.800Z"
